{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And if thus You do to me.</b> Moses' strength failed like a woman's when the Holy One, blessed be He, showed him the punishment He was destined to bring upon them on this account. He said before Him: If so, kill me first." "<b>And let me not see my affliction.</b> It should have written בְּרָעָתָם — 'their affliction'; but Scripture used a euphemism, and this is one of the tikunim of the scribes in the Torah — a euphemism and an adjustment of language."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:20.388269258Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}